type: software
title: "Asymptotic permanental dominance at fixed Gram rank"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. For Gram matrices of n vectors in a space of fixed dimension d, the normalised first and second moments of every non-trivial Schur-power block (ordinary immanants and Lavi's quadratic version) tend to zero as n grows, uniformly over all shapes, so Lieb's permanental dominance inequality for ordinary immanants and Lavi's quadratic inequality hold at each fixed rank for all sufficiently large n (threshold not computed). The standard block is eventually the worst, with complex-rank moments asymptotic to (d-1) log n / n and (d-1)(log n)^2 / n. Growing-rank ranges and explicit bounds for the standard block at every n and d are also given."
